1
00:00:05,764 --> 00:00:07,234
Now! Listen, Kobato!

2
00:00:07,234 --> 00:00:10,104
"Summer vacation" is our competition!

3
00:00:10,244 --> 00:00:12,144
Our... competition?

4
00:00:12,144 --> 00:00:17,714
That's right! Summer vacation means
beaches! Camping! Outdoor parties!

5
00:00:17,714 --> 00:00:22,814
It is filled with all sorts of
distractions from hurt and pain.

6
00:00:23,324 --> 00:00:24,944
Hey Dobato! Are you listening to me?!

7
00:00:28,554 --> 00:00:29,724
A letter...

8
00:00:29,724 --> 00:00:32,424
That is not a letter! It's a flyer! A flyer!

9
00:00:34,394 --> 00:00:39,334
What did I tell you? Kompeito
collecting isn't going to be easy.

10
00:00:39,864 --> 00:00:42,174
Watch out especially for summer festivals.

11
00:00:42,174 --> 00:00:42,334
Summer Festival Notice
Sakura Park August 14, 15
Watch out especially for summer festivals.

12
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:42,374
Summer Festival Notice
Sakura Park August 14, 15

13
00:00:42,374 --> 00:00:45,074
Summer Festival Notice
Sakura Park August 14, 15
Flutes and drums, street vendors and yukata.

14
00:00:45,074 --> 00:00:45,174
Summer Festival Notice
Sakura Park August 14, 15
They've even got folk dancing.

15
00:00:45,174 --> 00:00:47,244
They've even got folk dancing.

16
00:00:47,244 --> 00:00:48,904
It's beautiful...

17
00:00:49,714 --> 00:00:51,204
Now listen, Kobato!

18
00:00:52,084 --> 00:00:54,574
I'm sure you already understand
what I'm trying to tell you!

19
00:00:59,724 --> 00:01:01,744
I am not finished!

20
00:01:02,324 --> 00:01:04,224
I won't let summer festivals get in the way.

21
00:01:04,524 --> 00:01:07,694
I will heal everybody's broken hearts!

22
00:01:13,604 --> 00:01:16,744
Kobato.

23
00:01:16,744 --> 00:01:19,574
Kobato.
What should I do?

24
00:01:19,574 --> 00:01:23,974
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

25
00:01:24,884 --> 00:01:28,184
Are always such a challenge

26
00:01:28,184 --> 00:01:30,954
I want to laugh when I'm happy

27
00:01:30,954 --> 00:01:35,254
And sing whenever I want

28
00:01:35,824 --> 00:01:38,254
Is all

29
00:01:39,564 --> 00:01:43,934
They say my dreams will come true someday

30
00:01:44,364 --> 00:01:47,634
But when will "someday" come?

31
00:01:47,634 --> 00:01:51,124
I can't wait forever

32
00:01:51,274 --> 00:01:57,044
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

33
00:01:57,044 --> 00:02:02,254
And let the light gather around me

34
00:02:02,254 --> 00:02:05,084
Where is it?

35
00:02:05,084 --> 00:02:08,424
Please tell me what I can do

36
00:02:08,424 --> 00:02:11,264
I make the most of getting hurt

37
00:02:11,264 --> 00:02:14,164
And run with all my might

38
00:02:14,164 --> 00:02:18,134
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

39
00:02:18,134 --> 00:02:21,174
And start crying

40
00:02:21,174 --> 00:02:25,194
I surprise myself

41
00:02:25,674 --> 00:02:29,834
In how much I believe in tomorrow

42
00:02:39,584 --> 00:02:43,024
...Memories of Summer.

43
00:02:47,534 --> 00:02:49,084
Summer festival...

44
00:02:52,034 --> 00:02:54,264
Where could it have flown to?

45
00:02:54,974 --> 00:02:56,374
Is this what you're looking for?

46
00:02:57,004 --> 00:02:58,974
Yes, that's it!

47
00:02:59,674 --> 00:03:01,644
Thank you very much!

48
00:03:02,514 --> 00:03:03,804
Just a minute.

49
00:03:04,544 --> 00:03:05,774
Here, use this.

50
00:03:06,954 --> 00:03:08,574
Your hands are soaking wet.

51
00:03:10,954 --> 00:03:12,784
Thank you very much.

52
00:03:14,454 --> 00:03:16,254
What is she up to now?

53
00:03:17,294 --> 00:03:19,624
It's a flyer for a summer festival.

54
00:03:20,064 --> 00:03:22,254
It's already that season, is it?

55
00:03:22,534 --> 00:03:24,224
Have you ever been to one?

56
00:03:24,334 --> 00:03:26,164
Every summer, since I was a child.

57
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:29,104
Portable shrines, fairs... and the fireworks
are like blooming flowers lighting up.

58
00:03:29,274 --> 00:03:30,604
Lit up?

59
00:03:33,714 --> 00:03:35,044
But...

60
00:03:35,944 --> 00:03:37,774
Maybe I won't be going this year.

61
00:03:38,044 --> 00:03:39,774
Why not?

62
00:03:40,084 --> 00:03:42,814
Hey! When we get to the pool, let's race!

63
00:03:42,814 --> 00:03:45,284
Okay! I'm not going to lose to you!

64
00:03:45,284 --> 00:03:48,694
Oh yeah? But you know what,
I can swim a little now.

65
00:03:48,694 --> 00:03:49,554
Really?

66
00:03:52,194 --> 00:03:55,594
I've got to get to my high school.
It's school day today.

67
00:03:55,594 --> 00:03:57,864
Yomogi Kindergarten is on summer vacation!

68
00:04:04,274 --> 00:04:05,404
Yukino.

69
00:04:06,474 --> 00:04:08,844
Natsuki! Good morning.

70
00:04:12,284 --> 00:04:14,584
You were walking with your eye on your
cell phone again, weren't you?

71
00:04:15,014 --> 00:04:17,214
Better hurry, or you're going to be late.

72
00:04:24,124 --> 00:04:25,754
Are you all right?

73
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:33,434
Kobato...

74
00:04:34,774 --> 00:04:36,234
Ioryogi-san!

75
00:04:36,904 --> 00:04:38,844
I feel heavy...

76
00:04:42,574 --> 00:04:44,114
Are you okay?

77
00:04:44,114 --> 00:04:45,414
No, I am not okay!

78
00:04:45,414 --> 00:04:48,054
And you. You're losing to
summer festivals already.

79
00:04:48,054 --> 00:04:51,454
Stay still. I'm going to help you get fired up!

80
00:04:58,794 --> 00:04:59,984
Hang me out to dry.

81
00:05:02,864 --> 00:05:05,124
That's the Seinan Women's
High School uniform.

82
00:05:05,304 --> 00:05:08,734
Do you know Natsuki, Fujimoto?

83
00:05:08,904 --> 00:05:09,834
No.

84
00:05:10,274 --> 00:05:12,004
It's the high school attached to
Seinan Women's University.

85
00:05:12,304 --> 00:05:14,674
It's where Ms. Sayaka and
Ms. Chitose graduated from.

86
00:05:14,974 --> 00:05:16,964
You know everything.

87
00:05:17,214 --> 00:05:18,484
It's a school for proper girls.

88
00:05:18,484 --> 00:05:19,944
Not any place you would've been involved with.

89
00:05:20,254 --> 00:05:21,974
He's mean again today too.

90
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:24,744
It's summer vacation at the kindergarten.

91
00:05:24,824 --> 00:05:27,844
He's probably spending his entire
holiday working and studying.

92
00:05:29,294 --> 00:05:32,314
By the way, it's dry. You're going
to return it, aren't you?

93
00:05:32,594 --> 00:05:33,964
That's right!

94
00:05:46,574 --> 00:05:49,014
Natsuki doesn't seem to be here.

95
00:05:49,144 --> 00:05:51,234
Better hurry before the sun goes down.

96
00:05:52,484 --> 00:05:54,354
There will be an official
announcement next term...

97
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:55,684
There she is!
There will be an official
announcement next term...

98
00:05:55,684 --> 00:05:56,814
There will be an official
announcement next term...

99
00:05:56,914 --> 00:06:00,024
but the volunteer club led by Natsuki
Mizuhashi has been recognized

100
00:06:00,024 --> 00:06:02,854
by the prefectural government for its
involvement in community beautification.

101
00:06:03,424 --> 00:06:07,194
There will be an award.

102
00:06:09,164 --> 00:06:13,224
So Natsuki's last name is Mizuhashi.

103
00:06:13,604 --> 00:06:15,904
The one that wiped out is also in the same class.

104
00:06:17,574 --> 00:06:20,244
And just because you're on vacation
doesn't mean you can stay up all night.

105
00:06:20,244 --> 00:06:21,364
Oh, from this morning...
And just because you're on vacation
doesn't mean you can stay up all night.

106
00:06:21,574 --> 00:06:23,544
Summer is an easy time to lose control.

107
00:06:23,744 --> 00:06:25,844
Remember that you are students
of Seinan Women's High School.

108
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:27,614
Behave accordingly, and...

109
00:06:28,684 --> 00:06:30,844
Yukino! You again?!

110
00:06:30,954 --> 00:06:32,944
If you don't stop it, I'll have
to take that from you.

111
00:06:33,624 --> 00:06:36,094
S-Sorry ma'am.

112
00:06:36,724 --> 00:06:40,624
Well then, I'm now confirming the emergency
contact network for summer vacation.

113
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:43,164
Hey! Came out pretty good!

114
00:06:43,294 --> 00:06:45,064
You've got talent.

115
00:06:45,504 --> 00:06:47,024
You think so?

116
00:06:47,204 --> 00:06:49,034
Have more confidence in yourself.

117
00:06:49,404 --> 00:06:50,424
That's all.

118
00:06:51,774 --> 00:06:56,144
Now, those of you in charge of cleaning
the pool, gather at the poolside.

119
00:06:56,514 --> 00:06:57,534
She's coming.

120
00:06:58,444 --> 00:06:59,814
Yes!

121
00:07:05,784 --> 00:07:07,014
Excuse me!

122
00:07:08,694 --> 00:07:10,424
Are you a student here?

123
00:07:10,994 --> 00:07:14,554
No. I'm Kobato Hanato of Yomogi Kindergarten.

124
00:07:14,734 --> 00:07:16,854
Kindergarten? What are you saying?

125
00:07:17,134 --> 00:07:20,394
You over there. Hurry and get
someone from the office, will you?

126
00:07:20,804 --> 00:07:22,824
Oh what a hassle. Kobato, run!

127
00:07:22,974 --> 00:07:24,834
What? But why?

128
00:07:24,904 --> 00:07:26,304
Just do as I say and run!

129
00:07:26,704 --> 00:07:28,574
Okay, I'll try.

130
00:07:29,514 --> 00:07:31,634
Where are you going?!

131
00:07:34,114 --> 00:07:37,314
Anyway, I have to find Natsuki.

132
00:07:42,494 --> 00:07:44,224
Hold on to the lens firmly.

133
00:07:44,364 --> 00:07:46,824
Nothing beats the real thing.

134
00:07:46,824 --> 00:07:49,824
You'll be able to afford one soon too, Yukino.

135
00:07:54,534 --> 00:07:57,094
That girl was with Natsuki this morning.

136
00:07:58,674 --> 00:08:00,804
Your name is Yukino?

137
00:08:00,974 --> 00:08:02,074
Yeah.

138
00:08:02,074 --> 00:08:04,134
I'm Kobato Hanato.

139
00:08:09,554 --> 00:08:10,714
Natsuki.

140
00:08:13,994 --> 00:08:17,014
This girl came looking for you.

141
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,364
Oh. From this morning.

142
00:08:19,364 --> 00:08:22,954
I, Kobato Hanato, have come
to return your handkerchief!

143
00:08:27,004 --> 00:08:28,304
You washed it for me?

144
00:08:28,304 --> 00:08:30,904
Yes. But I don't own an iron.

145
00:08:30,904 --> 00:08:32,774
I'm sorry for all the wrinkles.

146
00:08:33,044 --> 00:08:36,134
Oh don't worry. Thank you very much.

147
00:08:37,444 --> 00:08:39,644
W-Well then, I'm off.

148
00:08:39,744 --> 00:08:42,014
What? But what about cleaning the pool?

149
00:08:42,014 --> 00:08:46,354
Sorry Natsuki. I didn't tell you. I've got a job.

150
00:08:46,554 --> 00:08:49,754
That's against school rules. You can't work.

151
00:08:51,064 --> 00:08:52,684
I know... but...

152
00:08:54,164 --> 00:08:55,634
Yukino!

153
00:08:58,464 --> 00:08:59,864
Sorry we're late.

154
00:08:59,864 --> 00:09:02,634
It's okay. Natsuki, I'm really sorry.

155
00:09:03,074 --> 00:09:04,404
Yukino!

156
00:09:04,774 --> 00:09:08,104
Yukino's working really hard
to buy her own camera.

157
00:09:08,944 --> 00:09:13,344
We'll help clean the pool so let her go, okay?

158
00:09:15,754 --> 00:09:17,414
I didn't know.

159
00:09:21,624 --> 00:09:23,214
Um, Natsuki!

160
00:09:25,464 --> 00:09:27,584
I-I'd like to join you!

161
00:09:30,564 --> 00:09:30,804
Mizuhashi

162
00:09:30,804 --> 00:09:33,034
Mizuhashi
Fujimoto was right.

163
00:09:33,034 --> 00:09:33,594
Fujimoto was right.

164
00:09:33,974 --> 00:09:37,994
This place really is out of my league.

165
00:09:38,774 --> 00:09:42,734
But telling her you'd like to join her.
Is there a more direct pickup line?

166
00:09:43,514 --> 00:09:46,814
Pickup line? Was it rude?

167
00:09:48,784 --> 00:09:49,914
Sorry to keep you.

168
00:09:50,454 --> 00:09:53,444
Um. Sorry for abruptly using
a line to pick you up!

169
00:09:56,894 --> 00:10:00,534
I didn't feel like coming home by myself.

170
00:10:00,534 --> 00:10:01,794
So I was happy.

171
00:10:02,534 --> 00:10:04,094
I'm glad.

172
00:10:07,004 --> 00:10:08,564
That photo...

173
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:12,464
It looks like Yukino.

174
00:10:13,344 --> 00:10:16,674
That's when we were in elementary
school. A summer festival.

175
00:10:16,944 --> 00:10:18,914
She's your best friend.

176
00:10:19,614 --> 00:10:22,044
She was... I guess.

177
00:10:22,984 --> 00:10:25,414
She isn't your best friend anymore?

178
00:10:27,394 --> 00:10:30,554
Well because she avoids me.

179
00:10:34,234 --> 00:10:35,824
Good morning, Natsuki!

180
00:10:36,194 --> 00:10:39,824
Morning, Yukino. Hey your shirt's
sticking out at back.

181
00:10:40,064 --> 00:10:41,094
What?!

182
00:10:41,304 --> 00:10:42,734
Let me fix it for you.

183
00:10:44,274 --> 00:10:48,004
We went to school together every day.

184
00:10:49,514 --> 00:10:50,984
Sorry I'm late.

185
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:53,034
Look at your hair, Yukino!

186
00:10:53,314 --> 00:10:55,154
Is it sticking out?! I'll be right back!

187
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:56,144
What!

188
00:10:57,014 --> 00:10:59,784
Hurry back, Yukino!

189
00:11:00,424 --> 00:11:02,784
And then, I don't know when, but...

190
00:11:03,024 --> 00:11:06,764
Sorry Natsuki! I overslept! Go ahead without me!

191
00:11:06,764 --> 00:11:08,384
Mhm. See you at school.

192
00:11:09,334 --> 00:11:11,694
Then after we got into high
school, little by little...

193
00:11:12,764 --> 00:11:14,034
And then you know what?

194
00:11:15,574 --> 00:11:16,934
How beautiful...

195
00:11:20,844 --> 00:11:22,604
Sorry, Natsuki. You go ahead.

196
00:11:23,174 --> 00:11:24,974
R-Right.

197
00:11:27,684 --> 00:11:28,654
Yukino.

198
00:11:28,654 --> 00:11:31,644
If you're interested in photography,
why don't you join our club?

199
00:11:32,224 --> 00:11:34,594
But I don't know if I can handle club activities.

200
00:11:34,594 --> 00:11:36,124
Don't say that.

201
00:11:36,124 --> 00:11:37,664
At least come and take a look.

202
00:11:37,664 --> 00:11:38,564
Um, but...

203
00:11:38,564 --> 00:11:40,114
Yeah, come visit us.

204
00:11:42,364 --> 00:11:45,634
Now it's like, we're totally apart.

205
00:11:49,674 --> 00:11:55,334
I don't even know what
Yukino's thinking anymore.

206
00:12:17,834 --> 00:12:19,994
I'd like to help Natsuki.

207
00:12:20,204 --> 00:12:21,464
How?

208
00:12:21,734 --> 00:12:23,294
I don't know!

209
00:12:24,374 --> 00:12:26,934
You don't know?!

210
00:12:28,244 --> 00:12:31,704
Anyway, I'm going to go and talk with Yukino.

211
00:12:35,814 --> 00:12:37,344
Thanks for your help.

212
00:12:37,584 --> 00:12:40,144
I think we'll be ready in time
for the festival after all.

213
00:12:40,284 --> 00:12:41,584
Yes.

214
00:12:48,134 --> 00:12:49,594
Choose any one you like.

215
00:12:49,594 --> 00:12:52,364
I'm sorry to bother you during work.

216
00:12:52,734 --> 00:12:55,764
That's okay, I'm about finished
with this job anyway.

217
00:12:55,834 --> 00:12:57,324
Is that right?

218
00:12:57,774 --> 00:12:59,204
I've saved up enough money.

219
00:12:59,204 --> 00:13:02,474
I can finally buy the camera I want when they
begin that sale at the station building tomorrow.

220
00:13:02,574 --> 00:13:05,174
What about the one you had yesterday?

221
00:13:05,484 --> 00:13:06,574
Yesterday?

222
00:13:07,144 --> 00:13:08,444
Oh...

223
00:13:08,614 --> 00:13:10,414
That belongs to a friend.

224
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:13,514
I really wanted my own though,
so I got a job and saved up.

225
00:13:13,684 --> 00:13:16,024
That's very impressive, Yukino.

226
00:13:16,194 --> 00:13:18,954
It's a hobby that began when I started taking
pictures with the camera on my mobile.

227
00:13:19,194 --> 00:13:20,764
Now I'm totally involved.

228
00:13:20,764 --> 00:13:25,024
I'm a lot closer to the photography club
members now. We have similar interests.

229
00:13:25,564 --> 00:13:26,934
What about Natsuki?

230
00:13:26,934 --> 00:13:27,774
Huh?

231
00:13:27,774 --> 00:13:31,224
Don't you talk with her much?

232
00:13:32,174 --> 00:13:36,114
I've been friends with Natsuki
since we were kids.

233
00:13:39,684 --> 00:13:41,084
Matching phones.

234
00:13:41,284 --> 00:13:42,184
Yeah.

235
00:13:42,454 --> 00:13:44,324
Hey, let's go and get straps.

236
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:45,914
Let's get matching ones.

237
00:13:46,024 --> 00:13:49,424
But if we have the same straps we
won't be able to tell which is which.

238
00:13:49,824 --> 00:13:51,084
You're right.

239
00:13:53,324 --> 00:13:55,134
I'm going to get this one!

240
00:13:55,134 --> 00:13:56,794
Then I'm getting this one!

241
00:13:57,294 --> 00:13:59,304
Watermelon 'cause my name means summer!

242
00:13:59,304 --> 00:14:01,094
A snowman because my name means snow!

243
00:14:02,434 --> 00:14:04,594
So cute!

244
00:14:05,244 --> 00:14:06,504
Want to swap?

245
00:14:06,504 --> 00:14:07,494
Sure!

246
00:14:09,414 --> 00:14:10,944
I'll take good care of it!

247
00:14:10,944 --> 00:14:13,004
I'll look after mine, too!

248
00:14:17,754 --> 00:14:21,154
Don't you get along with Natsuki now?

249
00:14:22,924 --> 00:14:24,894
Don't you like her anymore?

250
00:14:24,964 --> 00:14:26,184
Of course I like her!

251
00:14:26,694 --> 00:14:28,684
How could I ever dislike Natsuki?

252
00:14:29,664 --> 00:14:31,824
She is my idol.

253
00:14:33,264 --> 00:14:35,664
Oh come on, you're embarrassing me!

254
00:14:37,434 --> 00:14:38,874
Let's take one together!

255
00:14:39,004 --> 00:14:40,164
Okay!

256
00:14:41,644 --> 00:14:43,334
Say cheese!

257
00:14:44,744 --> 00:14:46,784
Let me take a proper one next time, okay?

258
00:14:46,784 --> 00:14:49,614
After you improve your picture taking skills.

259
00:14:49,854 --> 00:14:51,544
What?!

260
00:15:06,234 --> 00:15:08,464
Natsuki and Yukino.

261
00:15:08,674 --> 00:15:11,574
They really want to remain the best of friends.

262
00:15:12,044 --> 00:15:14,204
Why aren't they able to do that?

263
00:15:14,574 --> 00:15:19,644
I don't know. How should I know if
even they can't figure it out?

264
00:15:20,544 --> 00:15:24,284
But... I wish there was something I could do.

265
00:15:26,824 --> 00:15:28,394
Summer Sale
Yomogi Station

266
00:15:28,394 --> 00:15:30,154
Summer Sale
Yomogi Station
Excuse me. Where is the camera shop
that's having a sale today?

267
00:15:30,154 --> 00:15:32,494
Excuse me. Where is the camera shop
that's having a sale today?

268
00:15:32,864 --> 00:15:34,024
To get there...

269
00:15:34,024 --> 00:15:35,154
Yes?

270
00:15:37,264 --> 00:15:40,164
Hey. Let's try taking some pictures
as soon as we get back.

271
00:15:40,164 --> 00:15:41,654
That's a great idea.

272
00:15:44,274 --> 00:15:45,334
Natsuki...

273
00:15:45,644 --> 00:15:46,944
Shopping?

274
00:15:46,944 --> 00:15:48,604
Uh, yeah.

275
00:15:49,344 --> 00:15:51,334
A single-lens reflex camera.

276
00:15:52,984 --> 00:15:54,444
Oh.

277
00:15:56,054 --> 00:15:59,984
Y-Yukino worked really hard to save
up and buy a great camera.

278
00:16:00,254 --> 00:16:01,354
That's right.

279
00:16:01,354 --> 00:16:03,654
The club members are all jealous.

280
00:16:03,654 --> 00:16:06,464
Yeah, so Yukino why don't
you join our photo club?

281
00:16:06,464 --> 00:16:08,294
Hey, good idea!

282
00:16:08,294 --> 00:16:10,904
To celebrate your SLR camera debut!

283
00:16:10,904 --> 00:16:13,364
I mean, you finally got that
camera you wanted so badly.

284
00:16:13,364 --> 00:16:16,274
I know. Let's go to a photo
session sometime soon.

285
00:16:16,274 --> 00:16:19,374
With your talent, Yukino, you'll
be sure to get good shots.

286
00:16:19,374 --> 00:16:20,544
Yes, lets!

287
00:16:20,544 --> 00:16:21,144
Right?

288
00:16:21,144 --> 00:16:22,014
Right!

289
00:16:22,014 --> 00:16:23,134
This is ridiculous!

290
00:16:26,344 --> 00:16:31,324
I mean, photos can look pretty good just by
copying the composition used in ads.

291
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:33,374
Too many people mistake that with talent.

292
00:16:34,224 --> 00:16:36,314
And that includes you, Yukino.

293
00:16:37,194 --> 00:16:41,684
I hate amateurs who think they're professional
when they don't even have what it takes.

294
00:16:48,034 --> 00:16:49,474
Yukino!

295
00:16:49,634 --> 00:16:50,904
Natsuki!

296
00:17:03,214 --> 00:17:04,584
Yukino.

297
00:17:11,594 --> 00:17:14,424
Sure, I wish I had talent.

298
00:17:15,164 --> 00:17:21,364
But right now I just enjoy taking pictures.
I love photography. That's all.

299
00:17:22,474 --> 00:17:28,274
Um... well... I'm happy for you that you were
able to buy that camera you like. Oh and...

300
00:17:28,274 --> 00:17:29,744
I'm sorry.

301
00:17:31,514 --> 00:17:33,204
Would you let me be alone?

302
00:17:42,524 --> 00:17:44,994
Why did I say that?

303
00:17:49,494 --> 00:17:53,054
It's gone. The strap is gone. Why?

304
00:17:59,974 --> 00:18:01,494
It's nowhere...

305
00:18:04,384 --> 00:18:06,684
Hey, where are you going now?

306
00:18:06,684 --> 00:18:12,274
That wasn't right for Natsuki to act the way she
did! I must go and have a word with her!

307
00:18:12,584 --> 00:18:13,914
And tell her what?

308
00:18:14,454 --> 00:18:18,414
Well, um... Anyway, I can't just
leave things like this!

309
00:18:27,974 --> 00:18:29,564
What's wrong?

310
00:18:30,674 --> 00:18:33,364
It's gone! My mobile strap! It's gone!

311
00:18:34,374 --> 00:18:35,904
I'll help you look for it!

312
00:18:37,574 --> 00:18:40,704
I've looked there. I've looked everywhere.
Over and over. It's gone!

313
00:18:41,154 --> 00:18:47,684
What am I going to do? It's because of all those
horrible things I said to Yukino, I know it.

314
00:18:49,224 --> 00:18:50,814
Anyway, I'll help you find it!

315
00:18:57,594 --> 00:19:02,294
What am I going to do?
What am I? What am I?

316
00:19:12,784 --> 00:19:14,304
Natsuki...

317
00:19:24,994 --> 00:19:26,514
Natsuki...

318
00:19:29,094 --> 00:19:30,564
I found it.

319
00:19:40,174 --> 00:19:41,574
Thank you!

320
00:19:42,274 --> 00:19:44,604
Thank you, Kobato!

321
00:19:48,414 --> 00:19:52,754
You and Yukino. You're still
best friends, aren't you?

322
00:19:54,524 --> 00:19:58,114
Maybe I was intimidated by Yukino a bit.

323
00:20:00,464 --> 00:20:06,124
Could that have been because she was so
beautiful working hard at what she likes?

324
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:12,864
Yukino has always been a bit different.

325
00:20:13,644 --> 00:20:16,474
Sometimes I'd look at her as
someone far out of my reach.

326
00:20:17,074 --> 00:20:20,644
I felt like she would leave me
behind. That scared me.

327
00:20:22,584 --> 00:20:26,854
That's why I had to work harder
with my studies and stuff.

328
00:20:29,894 --> 00:20:34,294
But I was the one that first pushed
Yukino away from me.

329
00:20:37,094 --> 00:20:40,534
Natsuki, may I borrow your phone?

